    "description": "    • Built as part of a duo a native iOS application in Swift which communicated with the backend API to allow users to stream and add music to their collection, organically discover new songs through other users in their network, and a variety of other features\n    • Transitioned codebase multiple times from Objective C through each version of Swift as well as updating the codebase and feature set to reflect the changes in each major release of iOS\n    • Created as part of a duo a native Android application in Kotlin, using Anko for views and layouts, which included all the same features as the iOS application\n    • Incorporated a heavily modified implementation of ExoPlayer in order to allow the full gamut of playback options users expect from a music player\n    • Built a custom view transition stack for pushing to and popping from views with a variety of different animations to avoid the overhead from creating full Activities for each view\n    • Spearheaded transition from monolithic Ruby on Rails application to a RESTful microservice based API written in Kotlin, allowing for significant gains in scalability and performance\n    • Worked closely with team to perform maintenance and ensure stability, reliability, and performance of all backend services\n    • Built in tandem with another developer a live audio broadcasting system which allows users to livestream audio from their iOS or Android device to an effectively unlimited number of listeners\n    • Helped design, organize, and implement core database functionality\n    • Utilized Jekyll, Bootstrap, and jQuery to build a clean, user-friendly website showcasing application features\n    • Designed and built an intuitive interface to allow users to upload music and edit file metadata",
